{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"# VibeCheck — Whole-Project Status\nSnapshot: 2026-07-30 (`main-demo` @ `5c65046` — **declared FINAL implementation**; future changes are bug fixes, not architecture) · FYP Group Epsilon, University of Moratuwa","x":-760,"y":-900,"width":1460,"height":100,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"verdict","type":"text","text":"## Overall verdict\n**The headline end-to-end claim is wired, demonstrated, and measured.** BPMN spec → M01 (LTLf property suite) → M02 (call-order WIR) → M03 (Phase A–D conformance check) → verdict + readable counterexample runs against real FLOW-BENCH LLM implementations (`demo/e2e_demo.py`), and a mutation-based E2E evaluation harness (`demo/eval_e2e/`) puts honest, CI-carrying numbers on it. Every module starts under docker-compose, every module has tests, and CI (PR #80) runs both.\n**First real run:** 29 eligible specs, 58 property checks — 100% agreement with M01's own `evaluate_ltlf` oracle on all 35 decisive verdicts; the 23 INCONCLUSIVEs are the atom-gate correctly refusing.","x":-760,"y":-740,"width":1460,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"m01","type":"text","text":"## Module 01 — Specification Analysis 🟢\n**Final:** 4-phase pipeline (~2,260 LOC) — dynamic semantic extractor with recovery pass, tiered LTLf synthesis, multi-round mutation self-healing + adversarial tier, and Phase 4 **PBCTS** (pure-Python LTLf progression → trace synthesis, BDA alignment, IDCD convergence, SCSL self-correction → Formal Reliability Certificate v2.0).\n**Cleanup day 2026-07-29:** startup crash fixed (`bc35c02`), **28 tests all pass** (PR #79), status codes unified on `PASS_PBCTS_UNCONVERGED` (PR #81), SPOT dropped from the Dockerfile (PR #82).\n**Wired handoffs:** `module_02_input.json` (task_patterns → M02) and `module_03_input.json` (LTLf suite → M03 `property_ingest`, PR #72).","x":-760,"y":-480,"width":700,"height":260,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"m02","type":"text","text":"## Module 02 — Verified IR Extraction 🟢 (most mature)\n~5,200 LOC · **256 tests** (169 tests/ + 87 eval/, verified 2026-07-29). **Measured:** genuine-bug detection 0.9952 (n=210) · false-alarm 0.0588 (n=51) · WIR structural F1 1.0 · natural-bug detection 1.0 strict / 0.9329 task_only.\n**This cycle:** call-order WIR (D2) exposed from `/verify` (PR #75 on #73); extract-engine container fixed — it had **never started** (sibling relative-import bug, PR #76); dominance-frontier infinite loop fixed (PR #85); V1-dominance caveat promoted to the prominent docs (PR #83).\n**Honest limits:** V2 ≈ no contribution on corpus; equivalent-mutant specificity 0.1111; numeric-boundary blind spot.","x":0,"y":-480,"width":700,"height":260,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"m03","type":"text","text":"## Module 03 — Equivalence Engine 🟢 (the documented method is executable AND wired)\n**C++/SPOT engine covers all phases A–D** (`lifter.cpp` 1,423 LOC); `process_wir_batch()` is the **declared canonical Phase D** (PR #77). **142 test functions** across 6 files.\n**This cycle:** M01 ingestion wired (`property_ingest.py`, PR #72 — tier-gated, Option B quoted atoms); **both vacuity channels closed** (atom-gate → INCONCLUSIVE PR #67; alive-extension LTLf→LTL bridge + mutual-exclusion edge closure PR #70); call-order lifting consumed (D2, PR #73) — fixes the definition-order defect; real FastAPI service `/lift` `/check` `/health` (PR #74).\n**Open:** loop-bound checking has no home in the canonical path; non-terminating-trace semantics deferred by design.","x":-760,"y":-180,"width":700,"height":270,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"m04","type":"text","text":"## Module 04 — Verification Portal 🟡\n573-line Streamlit app, 4 pages; **all three engine pages call their engines over HTTP** — the equivalence page (broken by construction at the previous snapshot) was fixed when M03 gained a real FastAPI service (PR #74). Unused `networkx` removed (PR #84). Sidebar dots are real health checks for all three engines.\n**Gaps:** zero tests; `POST /check` (full A–D conformance) has no UI demo — it needs a call-order-lifted WIR, which extract-engine's HTTP API now returns but the UI doesn't yet chain; PR #74 verification was local-only (compose build of SPOT unverified in that session).\nStill explicitly disclaims research novelty (integration layer).","x":0,"y":-180,"width":700,"height":270,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"strengths","type":"text","text":"## Strengths ✅\n- Sound dual-track independence (no circular verification) — preserved even in the bridge (ported, not imported, normalization)\n- End-to-end loop closed *and measured*, with abstention reported honestly instead of averaged away\n- Exceptional epistemic discipline: measured fact vs design intent labeled everywhere; every rate carries its CI; archived pre-fix reports as audit trail\n- Module 02 is legitimately good engineering (PEP 669 tracer, parity tests, timeouts, calibration)\n- Schema-first WIR contract; two views (definition-order + call-order) without breaking consumers\n- CI: per-module tests + a real docker-compose startup check (a class of bug that had bitten twice)","x":-760,"y":140,"width":700,"height":320,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"gaps","type":"text","text":"## Remaining gaps / risks ⚠️\n- Only the `node()`-free slice of P1 properties is conformance-checkable (**17.6%** of the tier, corpus-measured); P0/P2/P3 excluded with reasons\n- **Loop-bound safety checking has no home** in the canonical path (`P2_Quality_Limits` excluded; legacy `run_pipeline` is its only implementation)\n- Non-terminating traces vs termination-requiring properties: explicitly deferred design decision (vacuity-vs-divergence risk on record)\n- E2E detection 0.357 at small n — task-drop mutants often unobservable → honest abstention (0.462), not misjudgment\n- M04: zero tests, no `/check` UI demo\n- V2 symbolic ≈ no contribution on the current corpus — certificate is V1-driven (stated in prominent docs, PR #83)","x":0,"y":140,"width":700,"height":320,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"next","type":"text","text":"**If work resumes:** 1) widen the checkable property slice (event-lifecycle mapping so start/done atoms survive; P3 needs the X-operator bridge) 2) give loop-bound checking a home in `process_wir_batch` 3) chain extract-engine's `call_order_wir` into M04's `/check` page for a UI-driven full conformance demo 4) grow the E2E gold set beyond 6 specs to shrink the CIs 5) M04 smoke tests.","x":-760,"y":510,"width":1460,"height":110,"color":"6"}
	],
